      "content": "Vitamin C is an antioxidant, but taking extremely high doses can cause harm, especially if your kidneys are not functioning optimally. While it does help boost the immune system, it won't necessarily treat a bacterial UTI effectively and could potentially lead to side effects like kidney stones or gastrointestinal issues. Considering your kidney disease, it's especially risky to alter your medication or dosages without professional guidance. Please definitely reach out to your doctor or a healthcare professional immediately, even if it's through telehealth services, for safe and appropriate advice. They will know the best course of action tailored to your specific health needs.",
